# The 7-Minute Workout
@description The classic circuit of twelve exercises, thirty seconds each with ten seconds' rest
  between them, from Klika and Jordan's 2013 article for the American College of Sports Medicine.
  You need a wall and a sturdy chair. Each exercise is a chapter, so you can repeat the circuit's
  hardest ones or skip any you can't do; push-ups and crunches ask for your count.
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout hiit
@rest 0:10
@artwork data:image/jpeg;base64,

@define [go]:
  @tone{pitch 988 Hz, length 0:00.15, volume 0.5}
  +0:00.05 @tone{pitch 1318 Hz, length 0:00.45, volume 0.5}

@define [stop]:
  @tone{pitch 440 Hz, length 0:00.25, volume 0.5}
  +0:00.15 @tone{pitch 440 Hz, length 0:00.25, volume 0.5}

// Three ticks a second apart, ending a second after the last: the exercise starts on the beat.
@define [countdown]:
  @tone{pitch 880 Hz, length 0:00.12, volume 0.5}
  +0:00.88 @tone{pitch 880 Hz, length 0:00.12, volume 0.5}
  +0:00.88 @tone{pitch 880 Hz, length 0:00.12, volume 0.5}
  +0:00.88

## Jumping jacks
The seven-minute workout: twelve exercises, thirty seconds each. First, jumping jacks.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Stay light on your toes.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Wall sit
Wall sit. Back flat against the wall, knees bent to a right angle.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Keep the thighs level.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Push-ups
@track Reps
Push-ups. Hands under the shoulders, body in a straight line. Count them.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Drop to your knees if you need to.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Crunches
@track Reps
Crunches. On your back, knees bent. Lift the shoulders, not the neck. Count them.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Breathe out as you lift.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Step-ups
Step-ups onto the chair. Step up with one leg, then the other, and down the same way.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Lead with the other leg.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Squats
Squats. Feet shoulder-width apart, sit back, chest up.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Down until the thighs are level.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Triceps dips
Triceps dips on the chair. Hands on its edge behind you, lower the hips, and push back up.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Elbows straight back, not out.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Plank
Plank. On your forearms, body straight from head to heels.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Don't let the hips sag.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## High knees
High knees. Run on the spot, knees up to hip height.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Drive the arms.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Lunges
Lunges. Step forward until both knees are at a right angle, alternating legs.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Front knee over the ankle.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Push-up and rotation
Push-up and rotation. After each push-up, turn into a side plank with one arm to the ceiling. Alternate
sides.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Keep the hips high as you turn.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Side plank
Last one: side plank. On one forearm, hips up, body straight. You'll switch sides halfway.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Switch sides.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]
+0:00.5 That's the seven minutes. Well done.

